back:'← Back to ARES',title:'Can someone explain the decision?',intro:'A five-minute, facilitator-led comprehension test. Invite someone outside the project and observe before helping. Repeat with up to three people if time allows.',scope:'This page is a test protocol, not evidence that a user study has taken place. Observations are entered by the facilitator and are not independently verified.',setup:'Before the test',setup1:'Open ARES in a separate tab. Start with 240 min available, 2.5 km/h pace, 30 min science work, 45 min reserve, and 12° slope limit.',setup2:'Do not start the guided demo before the tasks. Avoid explaining which route the person should choose.',setup3:'Read one task at a time. Record whether the person completes it unaided, with help, or not at all.',open:'Open ARES in another tab ↗',print:'Print protocol',code:'Anonymous participant code (optional)',privacy:'Use a code, not a name or email. Nothing is uploaded. Export saves a file on your device; unfinished notes are lost if you close the page.',task1Title:'Compare the two routes',task1:'Ask the person to identify the science destination, the route with the lower mapped slope, and the route with more conservative reserve margin.',task2Title:'Change the reserve requirement',task2:'Ask the person to require 50 min of reserve while keeping the other settings unchanged. Which route meets that requirement in the conservative scenario, and why?',task3Title:'Interpret the result',task3:'Ask what the green result establishes, what the app does not validate, and one reason the person might reconsider a plan.',outcome:'Observed outcome',notes:'What did the person say or struggle with?',confirmation:'I am recording observations from an actual person. These are facilitator-entered notes, not independent scientific or safety validation.',export:'Export observation notes (JSON)',gate:"Export is enabled after all three outcomes are selected and the observation statement is confirmed. This does not update the project's validation claims.",keyTitle:'Facilitator reference — open after the tasks',key1:'Rochette is the target. The terrain route has lower maximum mapped slope; the direct baseline preserves more time.',key2:'With 50 min required reserve, the direct baseline has approximately +7.8 min margin; the terrain route has approximately −1.9 min in the conservative scenario.',key3:'Green means the configured reserve holds under the displayed assumptions. It does not certify operational safety or validate oxygen, radiation, weather, or unresolved obstacles.',after:'Use the difficulties you observe to revise wording or layout. Record what happened, including failures; do not infer a safety benefit from this small comprehension test.',footer:'No names, uploads, accounts, or automatic claims of human validation. ARES remains a research prototype.',empty:'Not observed',independent:'Completed unaided',help:'Completed with help',missed:'Not completed / incorrect explanation',saved:'Observation notes exported to your device.'
